{"name":"My Fair Lady","hex":"#f3c4c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Beautiful, of a pleasing appearance, with a pure and fresh quality.","Unblemished (figuratively or literally); clean and pure; innocent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something which is fair (in various senses of the adjective).","A woman, a member of the ‘fair sex’; also as a collective singular, women."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair"},{"term":"lady","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The mistress of a household.","A woman of breeding or higher class, a woman of authority."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To address as “lady”."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lady"}],"entries":[{"title":"My Fair Lady","blocks":[{"text":"My Fair Lady is a musical with a book and lyrics by Alan Jay Lerner and music by Frederick Loewe. The story, based on George Bernard Shaw's 1913 play Pygmalion and on the 1938 film adaptation of the play, concerns Eliza Doolittle, a Cockney flower girl who takes speech lessons from professor Henry Higgins, a phonetician, so that she may pass as a lady. Despite his cynical nature and difficulty understanding women, Higgins grows attached to her."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/97/Myfairlady.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Fair_Lady","wikidata":"Q591943"},{"title":"My Fair Lady (film)","blocks":[{"text":"My Fair Lady is a 1964 American musical comedy drama film adapted from Lerner and Loewe's 1956 stage musical based on George Bernard Shaw's 1913 stage play Pygmalion. With a screenplay by Alan Jay Lerner and directed by George Cukor, the film depicts a poor Cockney flower-seller named Eliza Doolittle who overhears phonetics scholar Henry Higgins casually wager that he could teach her to speak English so well she could pass for a duchess in Edwardian-era London, or secure employment in a flower store. It stars Audrey Hepburn as Doolittle, replacing Julie Andrews from the stage musical, and Rex Harrison as Higgins, reprising his role from the stage, with Stanley Holloway, Gladys Cooper and Wilfrid Hyde-White in supporting roles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/My_fair_lady_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Fair_Lady_(film)","wikidata":"Q201215"},{"title":"Fair Lady","blocks":[{"text":"FAIRLADY is a South African women's magazine that is often considered as the sister publication to the Afrikaans Sarie. With their offices in Cape Town, this title is one of the most popular female reads in South Africa."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_Lady","wikidata":"Q5429841"},{"title":"Fair","blocks":[{"text":"A fair is gathering of people for a variety of entertainment or commercial activities. Fairs are typically temporary with scheduled times lasting from an afternoon to several weeks. Fairs showcase a wide range of goods, products, and services, and often include competitions, exhibitions, and educational activities. Fairs can be thematic, focusing on specific industries or interests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/2008Overview1.JPG/330px-2008Overview1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair","wikidata":"Q288514"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/MusicalTheater3.jpg/500px-MusicalTheater3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/MusicalTheater3.jpg/500px-MusicalTheater3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Program from Mark Hellinger Theatre","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMusicalTheater3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/My_Fair_Lady_Berlin.jpg/500px-My_Fair_Lady_Berlin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/My_Fair_Lady_Berlin.jpg/1280px-My_Fair_Lady_Berlin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/My_Fair_Lady_Berlin.jpg/500px-My_Fair_Lady_Berlin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Berlin, 1961","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMy_Fair_Lady_Berlin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Harry_Stradling-Audrey_Hepburn_in_My_Fair_Lady.jpg/330px-Harry_Stradling-Audrey_Hepburn_in_My_Fair_Lady.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Harry_Stradling-Audrey_Hepburn_in_My_Fair_Lady.jpg/330px-Harry_Stradling-Audrey_Hepburn_in_My_Fair_Lady.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cinematographer Harry Stradling and Audrey Hepburn as Eliza Doolittle on set of the film","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarry_Stradling-Audrey_Hepburn_in_My_Fair_Lady.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/My_Fair_Lady_Audrey_Hepburn.jpg/500px-My_Fair_Lady_Audrey_Hepburn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/My_Fair_Lady_Audrey_Hepburn.jpg/1280px-My_Fair_Lady_Audrey_Hepburn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/My_Fair_Lady_Audrey_Hepburn.jpg/500px-My_Fair_Lady_Audrey_Hepburn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb